# Root .dockerignore (R2.8: hub image must not bake secrets).
# The legacy Docker builder (no buildx) ignores packages/hub/Dockerfile.dockerignore,
# so without this file `docker build -f packages/hub/Dockerfile .` would send
# gitignored local files (unscrubbed fixtures/raw, .env*, probe.json, sqlite data)
# into the build context. Deny everything, allow only what the hub build needs.
# This file is deny-all for every Docker build whose context is the repo root.
# Any future image built from the root must add its paths to the allow-list here.
# Keep in sync with packages/hub/Dockerfile.dockerignore and infra/web/Dockerfile.dockerignore.
*
!package.json
!pnpm-lock.yaml
!pnpm-workspace.yaml
!tsconfig.base.json
!packages/contract/package.json
!packages/contract/tsconfig.json
!packages/contract/src
!packages/hub/package.json
!packages/hub/tsconfig.json
!packages/hub/src
!packages/hub/scripts/bundle.mjs
# Web image (infra/web/Dockerfile): only what its COPY lines reference.
!packages/web/package.json
!packages/web/tsconfig.json
!packages/web/index.html
!packages/web/vite.config.ts
!packages/web/tailwind.config.ts
!packages/web/postcss.config.js
!packages/web/playwright.config.ts
!packages/web/src
!packages/web/scripts
!packages/web/e2e/*.ts
!infra/web/nginx.conf
!infra/web/05-validate-sd-env.sh

# Re-exclude sensitive material even inside allowed directories (last match wins).
**/.env*
**/probe.json
**/*.sqlite*
**/node_modules
**/fixtures/raw
